From 93665cd3240f923b594ba4e05308bab121e2864a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:16:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: add the Wasm (WebAssembly) architecture

arch/wasm for a single-instance, single-threaded kernel whose user mode
is unmodified riscv64 Linux ELF, run by kwemu, a software CPU linked into
the kernel (KWEMU=libkwemu.a). The kernel is built with clang for
wasm64 (memory64) and links with wasm-ld; hvc_wasm is the console.

Based on Joel Severin's linux-wasm port ("wasm: Add support for Wasm
(WebAssembly)" and "wasm: hvc: Add Wasm console support", WIP v4,
joelseverin/linux branch wasm-7.0). This keeps that port's build
integration, low-level headers (atomics, barriers, cmpxchg, string),
linker script, boot and setup skeleton and hvc console, and leaves out
its NOMMU, Wasm-binfmt, SMP and wasm32 parts.

- Tasks: every task runs on its own Wasm stack. __switch_to calls the
  suspending JSPI import wasm_switch_to; new tasks start at the
  ret_from_fork export. UP with ARCH_NO_PREEMPT.
- MMU=y: Sv39-format user page tables (riscv PTE bits, 3 levels) walked
  by kwemu (asm/kw_emu.h, the contract with kwemu: KW_ABI_VERSION,
  checked at boot, and an 8 MiB struct kw_cpu, reserved statically) and
  by software uaccess. The kernel runs in the direct map, and vmalloc is
  VMALLOC_FLAT. kw_clear_reservation() on every context switch, signal
  delivery and sigreturn keeps LR/SC correct.
- riscv64 user ABI: the riscv syscall table through pt_regs wrappers,
  clone() argument order CLONE_BACKWARDS (musl's pthread_create() passes
  tls before child_tidptr), rt_sigframe/ucontext, ELF EM_RISCV, AT_HWCAP
  IMAFDC, uname riscv64, and a signal return page instead of a vDSO.
- Time: the timer is a one-shot deadline on the host monotonic clock,
  which also drives sched_clock. Timer, host IRQs (bits in
  wasm_host_irqs: console, net, block, sync, input, vsock, shm) and the
  host yield (every 20 ms) are checked when a 200k-instruction slice
  ends and in idle. The slice belongs to the CPU: each syscall and page
  fault charges it 1000 instructions, so a kernel-bound loop still sees
  timer ticks. irq_work runs from the tick (nothing raises an irq_work
  interrupt; Tiny SRCU needs it).
- Host interface: WASI preview 1 for the generic services (clocks,
  random_get, console fd_write/fd_read, poll_oneoff for idle,
  sched_yield, proc_exit for power-off, halt, restart and panic, the
  command line from args_get, and the initrd read from the file "initrd"
  in a preopened directory). Preview 1 is a wasm32 ABI, so pointer
  arguments go through wasi_ptr() or static buffers below 4 GiB. The
  rest is module "unkernel"; kwemu's optional JIT imports its own three
  functions from there. The kernel derives the console IRQ from stdin
  readiness after idle and yield, for hosts that never write
  wasm_host_irqs.
- WASM_IRQ_SYNC: the host asks for ksys_sync() (a browser tab may go
  away), from a work item; requests coalesce.
- hvc_wasm takes the console window size from the host and resizes the
  tty (SIGWINCH) when it changes.

Co-developed-by: Joel Severin <joel.severin@icemanor.se>
Signed-off-by: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
